      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "No assigned numerical exercise. From equal excess pressure derive F2=F1*A2/A1; incompressible volume gives s2=A1*s1/A2; multiplying gives equal ideal transmitted works. Distances are magnitudes and atmospheric loads cancel. Reviewer probe only: area ratio4,5N input and8cm stroke give20N,2cm and both works2/5J. Source explicitly neglects hydrostatic/inertial/dissipative corrections. Checking the excluded finite-head case gives missing output work rho*g*A1*s1²*(1+A1/A2)/2; it is not silently treated as zero for an arbitrary finite real stroke. Relative correction tends to zero with stroke. This lesson judgement does not change the separately failed original numerical E005 edition.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Confined incompressible liquid,ideal frictionless pistons,equal atmospheric reference,slow quasi-equilibrium operation,positive areas and normal load increments. The source explicitly neglects hydrostatic,inertial,dissipative corrections; equal-work formula is inside that model. Initial equal heights alone do not eliminate head changes of an arbitrary finite real stroke. Significant evolving head requires fluid gravitational energy,as independently quantified;source approximation is not universalized.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Separates pressure increment from force and atmosphere,states approximation assumptions,then derives inverse stroke ratio before ideal work balance. Warns against simultaneous force and displacement gain. Complete source includes direct permission to neglect hydrostatic corrections;that statement is not invented by reviewer. No numerical calculator requirement or student calibration.",
