      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "No assigned numerical exercise. Pressure on a submerged box gives upward force[p0+rho*g(d+H)-(p0+rho*g*d)]A=rho*g*A*H; constant background and depth cancel. With no other forces, equality to mean-body-density*Vtotal*g yields immersed fraction rho_body/rho_fluid. Reviewer probes only:600kg/m³ in1000kg/m³ gives3/5;1L fully submerged has buoyancy10N and weight6N for assignedg10,requiring4N downward tether. Closed hollow body30g with100mL external excluding-liquid volume has mean density300kg/m³ and floating displaced volume30mL,regardless of denser wall material.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Hydrostatic homogeneous fluid and approximately constant gravity,body not supported by bottom;buoyancy uses volume actually excluding liquid. Floating ratio assumes freely equilibrated body with only weight and liquid buoyancy,air neglected. Immersed fraction must lie[0,1];mean density greater thanfluid cannot satisfy free floating. Hollow-body external volume must exclude fluid,not include a flooded open cavity. Constraint forces must be included if held submerged,as source states.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Derives upward resultant from varying surface pressure and displaced-fluid substitution,then distinguishes complete immersion from free flotation. Uses mean density for hollow objects and explicitly requires adding constraint forces when held underwater. Displaced volume means excluded liquid,not every geometric interior regardless of flooding. No keyed answer substituted for reasoning.",
